## What is Allmaps?

Allmaps is an open source ecosystem for curating, georeferencing and exploring
digitized maps. Use <a href={toolIdentities.editor.href}>{toolIdentities.editor.name}</a> to place
historical maps in their geographical context, and
<a href={toolIdentities.viewer.href}>{toolIdentities.viewer.name}</a> to display them over a modern map.
Allmaps works with images published through IIIF by libraries, archives and museums.

Developers can use its [open source libraries and plugins](/open-source) to build their
own mapping tools and websites. The [open georeference data](/data) created with
Allmaps is available for anyone to download and reuse.

## What is the goal of Allmaps?

Allmaps aims to make every digitized map in the world easier to find and use,
across libraries, archives and museums. We bring georeference data together in a
shared, open database and provide open source tools for people to explore, work
with and build on these maps. There are millions of digitized maps available through IIIF, and you can help georeferencing them!

