## What is georeferencing?

Georeferencing connects places on a digitized map to their real-world locations.
In <a href={toolIdentities.editor.href}>{toolIdentities.editor.name}</a>, you mark matching points on the
historical map and a modern map.

Allmaps uses these control points to align the historical map with its surroundings,
so you can compare maps from different periods and see how places have changed.

<p class="mt-6">
  Learn how to place your first map with our
  <a href={`${docsBaseUrl}/guides/georeferencing-maps`}>guide to georeferencing</a>.
</p>

</div>

